From 9ee5226ccf04113afc6976b52e97de334f689eac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mrfelek <17274927+mrfelek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:37:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(agc): reuse data-only hit stages whose buffer bases
 moved

A data-only hit compiled a stage again whenever a used user word
differed, even when the word is only a buffer base and the data behind
the new base equals the cached runs. Such stages now reuse the cached
variant with its runs shifted, validated by content, and forwarded
words patched. Stages whose vertex fetch decode reads guest memory
become relocatable when every read names its user word.

APS5_NO_DATA_HIT_RELOCATION and APS5_NO_VERTEX_FETCH_RELOCATION turn
the two parts off. The draw-cache trace counts relocated stages.

AI-assisted. Tested by me on my own machine.
